[size=6][b]Complete Planet Survey[/b][/size]

Skip the planet survey grind. Scan a single flora or fauna, run one console command on a planet, or complete the [b]entire galaxy at once[/b] — survey data, traits, flora, fauna, and resources, all in one shot.

[line]

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]One planet, instantly[/b] — advances the current planet's survey to 100%: all flora, fauna, resources, and traits.
[*][b]The whole galaxy, one command[/b] — completes every planet and moon at once (~1798 bodies), with no fast-travel and no per-planet visiting.
[*][b]Persistent green flora & fauna[/b] — planets completed this way show their plants and creatures as scanned (green) when you land, including planets you have [i]never visited[/i], and it survives saving and reloading.
[*][b]Reveals all planet traits.[/b]
[*][b]Awards the "<Planet> Survey Data" slate[/b] to your inventory — the same reward a vanilla full survey gives.
[*][b]Biome Complete[/b] fires for every biome, not just the one you are standing in.
[*][b]Built-in instant scan[/b] — one scan completes a species, so natural scanning is faster too (no separate Instant Scan mod needed).
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/7589]Starfield Script Extender (SFSE)[/url] — required, and must match your game version.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/3256]Address Library for SFSE Plugins[/url] — required.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]How to use[/b][/size]

[b]Option 1 — Hand Scanner (auto-complete on scan)[/b]
Turn the toggle on:
[code]Settings → Gameplay → Complete Planet Survey → Auto-Complete Survey on Scan[/code]
Then open your scanner, point at any flora, fauna or resource, and Scan (E) as normal — the whole planet completes.

[b]Option 2 — Console, current planet[/b]
[code]cgf "CompletePlanetSurveyQuest.CompleteSurvey"[/code]
Be on a planet surface (not in a ship or interior). Works regardless of the toggle.

[b]Option 3 — Console, the entire galaxy[/b]
[code]cgf "CompletePlanetSurveyQuest.CompleteAllPlanetsSurveyData"[/code]
Completes every planet in the game in a single pass (it takes a minute or two and may briefly stutter). Afterwards, land on any planet — even one you have never visited — and its flora and fauna are already scanned and shown in green.

[line]

[size=4][b]Notes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The hand-scanner UI may not refresh until the area is reloaded; the survey data and the green scanned outlines are applied either way.
[*]Address Library keeps the mod resilient across game patches, but each release is built and tested against a specific game / SFSE build — check the changelog or sticky post for the tested version.
[/list]

[line]

